## The following text has been annotated for parts of speech by students at NTU Singapore as part of a class project in AY 2025-26.
## Verses are extracted from the taggedPBC. Annotations have been developed with a combination of manual and automated approaches, with reference to existing literature and (where possible) native speakers.
## ISO 639-3: tyz, Language: Tày, Number of verses: 21
## References: Day, A. C., & Day, J. (1962). Tày–Vietnamese dictionary (manuscript). SIL Global. https://www.sil.org/system/files/reapdata/72/44/19/72441920064367797993800063272833470595/tyz_Vietnamese_English_Dictionary.pdf ; Hirano, A. (2019). The differences between the Tày and Nùng languages in the Tràng Định District of Lạng Sơn Province. In Topics in Middle Mekong Linguistics (Journal of Research Institute, Vol. 60). Kobe City University of Foreign Studies. ; Lương, B. (Ed.), Nông, V. T., Lương, K. D., & Lê, H. G. (2011). Tày–Vietnamese dictionary (Code: 2011-DHTN 1201). Thai Nguyen University of Science. ; Ngoc, A. L. T., & Giang, G. L. T. H. (2023). Characteristics of words about the Tay people’s festival in Vietnam. International Journal of Multidisciplinary Research and Growth Evaluation, 4(6), 454–460. https://www.allmultidisciplinaryjournal.com/uploads/archives/20231124111300_F-23-07.1.pdf ; Phương, C. T. T. (2024). The Tày language in Tuyên Quang. International Journal of Research and Innovation in Social Science, 8(5), 2084–2088. https://doi.org/10.47772/IJRISS.2024.805151 ; Ratanakul, S. (2007). Tai peoples and their languages: A preliminary observation. Journal of Religion and Culture, 1(1), 189–232. https://www.yumpu.com/en/document/read/23824841/tai-peoples-and-theirs-languages-a-preliminary-khamkoo ; Wikipedia. (n.d.). Tày language. In Wikipedia. Retrieved April 12, 2026, from https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/T%C3%A0y_language ; Wikipedia. (n.d.). Wikitionary: The free dictionary. Tày language. Retrieved April 12, 2026, from https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki. ; World Mission. (n.d.). Tày language. Retrieved April 12, 2026, from https://worldmission.media/languages-of-the-world/tay.

